<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  my_boat_thruster_layout_v2.xacro
  ================================
  The vessel's **v2 (decoupled) propulsion ARRANGEMENT**: two centreline lateral
  thrusters straddling the centre of gravity — one FORWARD, one AFT — plus a
  fixed axial stern propeller. Sibling of my_boat_thruster_layout.xacro (v1:
  two bow tunnels side by side + a steerable stern drive), which is unchanged.

  Source of truth for the geometry:
    dynamic_positioning/claude/thruster_allocator_v2/config/allocator_v2.yaml
    dynamic_positioning/claude/thruster_allocator_v2/image/layout_v2.jpg

                     bow (+X)
                      /\
                     /  \
                    |    |
                    | T1 |   <===>   forward lateral   r1 = (+d1,  0  )
                    |    |
                    | oC |         centre of gravity = base_link origin
                    |    |
                    | T2 |   <===>   aft lateral       r2 = (-d2,  0  )
                    | P1 |     |     stern propeller   r3 = (-d3, p1_y)
                    |____|
                     stern (-X)

  All positions are in the my_boat/base_link (CG-centred) frame: x fwd, y port,
  z up.

    T1  fwd lateral : x=+d1  y=0     z=-0.23  yaw=+1.5708  (+cmd thrust +Y port)
    T2  aft lateral : x=-d2  y=0     z=-0.23  yaw=+1.5708  (+cmd thrust +Y port)
    P1  stern prop  : mount x=-d3 y=p1_y z=-0.25  yaw=+3.1416 (faces -X);
                      strut 0.40 m -> prop at z=-0.65; NO steering joint.

  Sign conventions for the downstream ROS 2 allocator (thruster_allocator_v2):
    * T1 > 0 and T2 > 0 BOTH thrust to PORT (+Y)   <- differs from v1!
    * P1 > 0 thrusts FORWARD (+X); P1 < 0 astern.
    * Resulting 3-DOF map, exactly the allocator's B:
          X = P1
          Y = T1 + T2
          N = d1*T1 - d2*T2 - p1_y*P1
      det(B) = -(d1 + d2) = -2.30 != 0  ->  full rank: pure sway and pure yaw are both
      commandable, and surge is decoupled from them.
    * d3 does NOT appear in B (an axial force on the centreline has no moment
      arm about Z); it only sets where the leg is drawn and where the pitch
      moment acts. p1_y != 0 is the parasitic-yaw-bias knob.

  ===========================================================================
  RETUNING THE STATIONS
  ===========================================================================
  d1 / d2 / d3 / p1_y are GLOBAL properties fed by <xacro:arg> from
  my_boat_gazebo_v2.urdf.xacro, so they can be overridden without editing any
  file:
      ros2 launch my_boat_gazebo my_boat_world_v2.launch.py d1:=1.90 d2:=1.40
      xacro my_boat_gazebo_v2.urdf.xacro namespace:=my_boat d1:=1.90 > boat.urdf
  KEEP THEM EQUAL TO allocator_v2.yaml — the allocator's B and the simulated
  hull must describe the same boat, or every yaw command is biased. The current
  defaults (1.40 / 0.90 / 1.40) mirror that file; it previously held the
  sketch-scaled 1.90 / 1.40 / 1.50, so re-check both after any change.

  ===========================================================================
  HULL-FIT CHECK  (measured off models/my_boat/mesh/my_boat_hull.stl)
  ===========================================================================
  Hull in base_link: bow tip x=+2.315, transom x=-1.854, keel z=-0.49.
  At the 420 kg equilibrium draft (~0.10 m, buoyancy.yaml) the waterline sits at
  z ~= -0.40, so the WETTED band of the hull is only x in [-0.95, +1.65]:

      station x   | +2.0  +1.9  +1.8  +1.7  +1.6  +1.5  +1.4  ... -0.9  -1.0
      keel z      | -0.22 -0.29 -0.33 -0.38 -0.42 -0.43 -0.45 ... -0.40 -0.37
      beam        |  0.75  0.89  0.99  1.09  1.18  1.26  1.32       1.79  1.59

  The current defaults put BOTH laterals inside that band: T1 at x=+1.40 (keel
  -0.45, hull beam 1.32) and T2 at x=-0.90 (keel -0.40, right at the aft edge of
  the wetted run). The earlier sketch-scaled stations (d1=1.90, d2=1.40) did
  not — the forefoot at x=+1.90 is 0.11 m ABOVE the waterline — which is why
  they were moved in. If you go back to them, expect the simulation to remain
  ideal (the gz Thruster plugin applies the commanded force regardless of
  submersion) while the real boat would ventilate; the trade is yaw authority,
  (d1+d2) 2.30 m -> 3.30 m, i.e. 225 -> 323 Nm at 98 N laterals.

  Two depths worth knowing, unchanged by the station choice:
    * lat_z = -0.23 is INSIDE the hull at both stations but ~0.17 m ABOVE the
      modelled waterline. At a 0.10 m draft this hull has no station deep enough
      to bury a 0.10 m tunnel; a real installation implies a deeper draft or
      externally mounted pods. Physics in gz is unaffected (force is applied at
      the link, submerged or not) apart from the roll arm.
    * P1's leg reaches z=-0.65, ~0.25 m BELOW the waterline, exactly like the v1
      stern drive, so it is genuinely in the water.
-->
<robot xmlns:xacro="http://ros.org/wiki/xacro" name="my_boat_thruster_layout_v2">

  <xacro:include filename="$(find my_boat_gazebo)/urdf/thrusters/my_boat_engine_v2.xacro"/>
  <!-- Physics macros are shared with v1 (thruster_force); steering_actuator is
       defined there too but deliberately NOT used — v2 has nothing to steer. -->
  <xacro:include filename="$(find my_boat_gazebo)/urdf/thrusters/my_boat_thruster_config.xacro"/>

  <!-- ===================== Mounting depths (base_link / CG frame) ========= -->
  <!-- Lateral thrusters: 0.23 m below the CG, same as the v1 bow tunnels. -->
  <xacro:property name="lat_z"        value="-0.23"/>
  <!-- Stern leg: hull mount 0.25 m below the CG, 0.40 m strut -> prop z=-0.65. -->
  <xacro:property name="p1_mount_z"   value="-0.25"/>
  <xacro:property name="p1_prop_drop" value="0.40"/>

  <!-- ===================== Hardware thrust limits (N) ===================== -->
  <xacro:property name="lat_max_thrust"   value="98.0"/>   <!-- APISQUEEN U92 Pro, 10 kgf -->
  <xacro:property name="stern_max_thrust" value="632.0"/>  <!-- Torqeedo Cruise 3.0 R -->

  <!-- ======================= T1: forward lateral ========================== -->
  <!-- yaw +90 deg: positive command thrusts +Y (port); lever +d1 -> +N -->
  <xacro:lateral_thruster prefix="T1" x="${d1}" y="0.0" z="${lat_z}" yaw="1.5708"/>
  <xacro:thruster_force name="T1" joint_name="T1_propeller_joint"
                        max_thrust="${lat_max_thrust}"/>

  <!-- ========================= T2: aft lateral ============================ -->
  <!-- yaw +90 deg: positive command thrusts +Y (port); lever -d2 -> -N -->
  <xacro:lateral_thruster prefix="T2" x="${-d2}" y="0.0" z="${lat_z}" yaw="1.5708"/>
  <xacro:thruster_force name="T2" joint_name="T2_propeller_joint"
                        max_thrust="${lat_max_thrust}"/>

  <!-- ==================== P1: fixed stern propeller ======================= -->
  <!-- yaw 180 deg: prop faces -X so positive command thrusts +X (forward).
       No steering joint and therefore no steering_actuator plugin. -->
  <xacro:stern_propeller prefix="P1" x="${-d3}" y="${p1_y}" z="${p1_mount_z}"
                         yaw="3.1416" prop_drop="${p1_prop_drop}"/>
  <xacro:thruster_force name="P1" joint_name="P1_propeller_joint"
                        max_thrust="${stern_max_thrust}"/>

</robot>
